Chapter: Fat32AllocCost

  cites Foreword chapter Fat32
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 Every sector read or written allocates one 512-byte buffer that stays until
 the heap mark is restored, so a write's heap delta counts its sector traffic.
 Files of 16, 32 and 48 clusters, each on a freshly formatted FAT32 volume
 (sector 2048, 20480 sectors) so that no write scans past another's clusters:
 a cost linear in the cluster count makes the second difference of the three
 deltas 0, and a chain walked from its head for every cluster added makes it
 positive. The same three files on one volume measure the free-cluster search:
 a search reading a sector per cluster it skips re-reads the earlier files'
 clusters and makes that difference positive too.

Section: Helpers

  zeros : Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zeros (n) (acc) = if list-length acc >= n then acc else zeros n (list-push acc 0)

  cost : Text, List Integer -> [Device.Block] Integer
  cost (name) (data) = act
    fmt <- fat32-format 2048 20480 "CODEX"
    vol <- fat32-init 2048
    let h = __heap-save
    in act
      w <- fat32-write-file vol name data
      __heap-save - h
    end
  end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing = act
    fmt <- fat32-format 2048 20480 "CODEX"
    vol <- fat32-init 2048
    let per = (vol.f32-sectors-per-cluster) * 512
    in let d16 = zeros (per * 16) []
    in let d32 = zeros (per * 32) []
    in let d48 = zeros (per * 48) []
    in act
      c16 <- cost "A16.BIN" d16
      c32 <- cost "A32.BIN" d32
      c48 <- cost "A48.BIN" d48
      print-line-uni ("second difference of the write costs " & show (c48 - 2 * c32 + c16))
      fmt2 <- fat32-format 2048 20480 "CODEX"
      vol2 <- fat32-init 2048
      s16 <- cost-on vol2 "B16.BIN" d16
      s32 <- cost-on vol2 "B32.BIN" d32
      s48 <- cost-on vol2 "B48.BIN" d48
      print-line-uni ("on one volume, second difference " & show (s48 - 2 * s32 + s16))
    end
  end

  cost-on : Fat32Volume, Text, List Integer -> [Device.Block] Integer
  cost-on (vol) (name) (data) =
    let h = __heap-save
    in act
      w <- fat32-write-file vol name data
      __heap-save - h
    end
